# Candidate packed rows of the nine restricted test forms

These are the first fifty rows and columns of the first nine adapted exterior
forms from the retained `discovery/saved/adapted.json`. The input SHA-256 is
`2b99f5cd9621db11b2ea806ff3efaf22794c97841a9267594023613c25a07b0a`.
See the polynomial certificate's `source/README.md` for its retained location,
the original ATLAS provenance, and the row convention.

This module publishes data only. Identifying these literals with
`restrictionTestForm` remains a separate proof obligation. Block zero of
`testFormRows` is the actual published pairing; the other blocks are these
candidate restrictions. Both the calibration proof and the polynomial
coefficient computation use this one table.
-/

